sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If the sides of the opposite planes of a cube are bisected, and the planes are carried through the points of section, then the intersection of the planes and the diameter of the cube bisect one another.
----
proof:

Let the sides of the opposite planes {CF|pCF} and {AH|pAH} of the cube {AF|cubeAF} be bisected at the points {K}, {L}, {M}, {N}, {O}, {Q}, {P}, and {R}, and through the points of section let the planes {KN|KLNM} and {OR|OPRQ} be carried. Let {US|SU} be the common section of the planes, and {DG} the diameter of the cube {AF|cubeAF}.

I say that {UT} equals {TS}, and {DT} equals {TG}.

Join {DU}, {UE}, {BS}, and {SG}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="360" height="340" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.38 diagram" src="propXI38.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
